~ start
if Global.read_book == false and Global.burnt_offering == false:
	A fire burning seemingly of it's own will. 
	Why would they keep a fire going inside of a small wooden building with no one to keep watch?
	The flames have a hypnotic rhythm to them.
	=> END
if Global.read_book == true and Global.burnt_offering == false:
	The book said the offerings "burn brightly".
	Does that mean I need to throw something into the fire?
	Wait, what am I thinking?
	I can't play along with this, this is nuts.
	But I'm so curious.
	- Offer a lock of hair
		I take the knife and slowly saw off a small length of hair. 
		I toss it into the flames.
		set Global.burnt_offering = true
		What the hell?
		=> END
	- Ofer a scrap of clothing
		I take the knife and gently cut off a piece of my shirt. 
		I toss it into the flames.
		set Global.burnt_offering = true
		What the hell?
		=> END
if Global.burnt_offering == true:
	The fire is now a blazing blue.
=> END